          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "Filum (Latin): thread or yarn. Traded in many materials (linen, cotton, wool, silk, worsted/crewel, and metal threads of gold, silver, copper and latten), colours, qualities, forms (skeins, bottoms, ribbon, wire) and uses (sewing, binding, piecing, packthread, sail-, net- and crossbow-thread), and from many places of manufacture (Cologne, Bruges, Oudenarde, Doornik, Burgundy, Prussia, Paris, Lyons, etc.)."
    }
  ],
